this is a dummy flasher for the binaries and spiff data needed for chorus32 timer

prequisites:
python3
esptool

lap timer:
plug in a battery. press button RST (hold it) -> PROG (hold it) -> release RST (while PROG hold) -> release PROG
now plug FTDI to the PROG pins

command line to run:
python naco_chorus32_flasher_final.py

binaries can be found in ../release_bins/
currenty i'm supporting flashing firmware.bin and spiff.bin, you will need to point to them both

